{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #241: declared status 'open'. Formalized: yes. Let $f(N)$ be the maximum size of $A\\subseteq \\{1,\\ldots,N\\}$ such that the sums $a+b+c$ with $a,b,c\\in A$ are all distinct (aside from the trivial coincidences). Is it true that\\[ f(N)\\sim N^{1/3}?\\] Current best: Bose and Chowla \\cite{BoCh62} provided a construction proving one half of this, namely\\[(1+o(1))N^{1/3}\\leq f(N).\\]The best upper bound known to date is due to Green \\cite{Gr01},\\[f(N) \\leq ((7/2)^{1/3}+o(1))N^{1/3}\\](note that $(7/2)^{1/3}\\approx 1.519$). Prize: $100. OEIS: A387704. Tags: additive combinatorics, sidon sets."},"claim_id":"vcl_febada2f5cc027484307f49df1c128336a80733a2b1aafe952c46a3ba350bfe9","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:241","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_ce91048ced024415","object_root":"sha256:6c3aedff426af64cc9779ade58af3e82dbd8be569be04bd67131f22b76e11d74","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_reco